# November 1 Acceptance Continuation

Status: two bounded local evidence gaps addressed; overall acceptance remains incomplete. No Skill source was changed in this continuation. Existing dirty source and historical trials remain preserved.

## Current Plan fallback behavior

One fresh context read the current `plan-handoff.md` owner and produced three responses. All three match the predeclared cause-specific codes: prohibited invocation → `dispatch_authorization_missing`; confirmed unavailable capability → `spec_doc_review_capability_unavailable`; ambiguous readiness → `worker_capability_unproven`.

The responses retain degraded/not-run status, distinguish supplied scenario facts from actual host discovery, and do not invent substantive self-review when no draft exists. Parent field checks and semantic review passed. See [protocol](protocol.json), [exact response](probe-response.txt), [trace](probe-trace.json), and [result](probe-result.json).

This is one context with three reporting cases, not three independent full Plan trials, a statistical result, live discovery, or a post-fix six-trial workflow evaluation. The original six Plan outputs and their defects remain unchanged.

## Debug-to-Simplify handoff

A new fresh consumer received the exact CEOPT-08-B1 repaired executable, original baseline, protected proof intent and original execution receipt. It read all three Simplify lenses inline and verified all eight source/proof pins. It proposed no change. It rejected removing report construction merely to save allocations because checksum equality alone does not establish complete report equivalence.

The parent admitted only the no-change proposal, copied baseline and repair into a disposable directory, and reran the original seven paired process cases: sizes 0, 1, 99, 101, and three 16000-entry runs. All expected checksums and output shapes matched; protected pins remained unchanged; cleanup was measured after directory removal. See [handoff](debug-simplify-handoff.json), [exact consumer response](simplify-response.txt), [provenance](simplify-provenance.json), and [process result](debug-simplify-process-result.json).

This establishes a mediated proof-preserving consumer handoff. It does not establish autonomous mutation, full-row equivalence, production performance, or a meaningful CEOPT-26 refactor. No change was manufactured to satisfy that facet. The consumer response is Chinese because its dispatch omitted the English artifact requirement; the unedited evidence is retained, while this report and new planning documents are English.

## Complete remaining-work reconciliation

All27 current scenario rows were reconciled against the durable owner map. Stale Commit/Plan/Tasks owner entries were updated to recognize completed October31 work. November1 Plan/Debug progress is reflected in current rows. [Remaining-work table](remaining-work.md) distinguishes feasible local follow-up from missing external targets.

Local work still includes meaningful protected refactoring, model-authored durable artifacts, differing-tree Worktree execution, knowledge publication recovery, PRD downstream consumption, orchestration recovery, genuine benchmark launches and executable Tasks. These are pending work, not automatically external blockers. Real PR/provider/media/Xcode/design/human facets require exact targets and evidence.

Historical remaining-27 accounting remains 175 attempts/170 finals, plus the separate October31 six-input-successor finals. This continuation adds two bounded consumer/probe contexts, kept separate from those trial counts. Both broader plans remain active. No project commit, push, global installation or runtime regeneration occurred.


